      "source": [
        "---\n",
"## Advanced Techniques\\n",
"\\n",
"Once you understand the basics, you can start composing tasks and handling\\n",
"cancellation and timeouts. For example, you can use `asyncio.wait_for` to\\n",
"enforce a timeout on slow operations, or `asyncio.create_task` to fire off\\n",
"background tasks.\\n",
"\n",
"In production code, it's common to wrap network calls (HTTP, DB, message\\n",
"queues) with async functions and orchestrate them using these primitives.\\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
"import asyncio\\n",
"\\n",
"async def slow_operation(name: str, delay: float) -> str:\\n",
"    await asyncio.sleep(delay)\\n",
"    return f\\"result from {name}\\"\\n",
"\\n",
"async def main_with_timeout() -> None:\\n",
"    try:\\n",
"        result = await asyncio.wait_for(slow_operation(\\"service\\", 2.0), timeout=1.0)\\n",
"        print(result)\\n",
"    except asyncio.TimeoutError:\\n",
"        print(\\"Timed out waiting for slow_operation()\\")\\n",
"\\n",
"print(\\"Try: asyncio.run(main_with_timeout())\\")\\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
"## Performance Considerations\\n",
"\\n",
"Asyncio is ideal for I/O-bound concurrency (network, disk, DB), not for\\n",
"CPU-bound work. For CPU-heavy tasks you should use processes or native\\n",
"extensions instead.\\n",
"\n",
"Typical patterns for performance:\n",
"- Use `asyncio.gather` to run many I/O-bound coroutines concurrently.\\n",
"- Use connection pools and keep-alive HTTP clients to reduce overhead.\\n",
"- Offload CPU-heavy code to threads/processes via executors.\\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
"import asyncio\\n",
"import time\\n",
"\\n",
"async def io_bound_task(delay: float) -> None:\\n",
"    await asyncio.sleep(delay)\\n",
"\\n",
"def compare_sync_vs_async(n: int, delay: float = 0.1) -> None:\\n",
"    \"\"\"Roughly compare total time for n sleep operations.\"\"\"\\n",
"    start = time.perf_counter()\\n",
"    for _ in range(n):\\n",
"        time.sleep(delay)\\n",
"    sync_elapsed = time.perf_counter() - start\\n",
"\\n",
"    async def _run():\\n",
"        await asyncio.gather(*[io_bound_task(delay) for _ in range(n)])\\n",
"\\n",
"    start = time.perf_counter()\\n",
"    asyncio.run(_run())\\n",
"    async_elapsed = time.perf_counter() - start\\n",
"\\n",
"    print(f\\"Sync total:  {sync_elapsed:.2f}s\\")\\n",
"    print(f\\"Async total: {async_elapsed:.2f}s\\")\\n",
"\\n",
"print(\\"Try: compare_sync_vs_async(10)\\")\\n"
      ]
    },
